INT. GENERATION SHIP "KESTREL" - CARGO HOLD C - NIGHT SHIFT

Stacked cryo-crates. Condensation drips from the ceiling. Cold light, long shadows. A hatch in the far wall is sealed with yellow tape.

TOMASZ, 50, crew chief, in a quilted jacket, leans against a crate. REN, 20s, logistics, holds a tablet. ASTRID, 40, a medic, kneels beside a cracked cryo-pod. BASHIR, 30s, an engineer, stands at the sealed hatch with a wrench.

TOMASZ
Count again.

REN
Two hundred twelve.

ASTRID
Two hundred eleven. This one's empty.

BASHIR
Two hundred ten. I counted the manifest.

TOMASZ
You don't count the manifest. You count the pods.

REN
The manifest says two hundred twelve.

BASHIR
The manifest is old.

ASTRID
This pod isn't cracked from the outside.

REN
What do you mean?

ASTRID
The glass bowed out. Someone woke up in here.

TOMASZ
Nobody wakes up. We don't wake until arrival.

BASHIR
Then someone did.

TOMASZ
Then someone's in this ship we don't know about.

REN
That's impossible.

ASTRID
So is the pod.

BASHIR
The hatch is taped from the inside.

They all turn to him. He taps the yellow tape with the wrench. It is peeled from the inside edge.

TOMASZ
Open it.

BASHIR
I'd rather not.

TOMASZ
Open it.

BASHIR
I'd rather you didn't.

Behind the hatch, someone knocks, once. Politely.
